  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provision of hygiene and sanitation services to South Sudanese Refugees in Al Salaam and Al Jabalain</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project seeks to provide sanitation and hygiene services and facilities to South Sudanese refugees in White Nile State in two localities (Al Salam and Al Jabalian localities). This project will mainly focus on improving sanitation and hygiene gaps/needs of South Sudanese refugees in the 10 camps in Al Salam and Al Jabalian localities, thereby reducing instances of water-borne or water-related diseases for 228,169  refugees in the 10 camps. Delivery of the project will be through rehabilitation of existing latrines, desludging of the existing communal latrines, construction of improved trench emergency communal latrines, construction of shared household/family latrines, decommissioning of out-of-use communal latrines, operation and maintenance of shared family latrines, communal and household latrines, provision of personal, household and community sanitation and hygiene services and capacity strengthening of sanitation and hygiene structures in the camps. The project is part and parcel of the priorities of the Sudan Country Refugee Response Plan (CRP), UNHCR Sudan Multi Year Strategy and WASH sector 2023 . The processes of project implementation will incorporate efforts and inputs of the Ministry of Health (MoH), Commissioner for Refugees (COR), the Water Environmental Sanitation Project (WES), UNHCR, UNICEF, WASH partners, and Humanitarian Aid Commission (HAC). Project design is informed by WASH sector strategies and recommendations.</narrative>
  </description>
